Regarding the possibility of bringing extinct species back to life, it is important to note that this is currently impossible. While the extraction and sequencing of ancient DNA can provide valuable information about extinct organisms, it is not possible to create a new organism from DNA alone. There are many other factors that are needed to create a new organism, such as a suitable host organism and a supportive environment.

However, the information gained from ancient DNA can help scientists understand the genetic and biological features of extinct organisms, which could be useful in the development of genetic engineering techniques that could be used to create organisms with certain desired characteristics.
