   \[
   32 \text{ lb} \times \frac{1 \text{ kg}}{2.22 \text{ lb}} = 17.1 \text{ kg}
   \]

2. Calculate the total dose of phenytoin:
   \[
   17.1 \text{ kg} \times 20 \text{ mg/kg} = 342 \text{ mg}
   \]

3. Calculate the infusion time:
   \[
   \frac{342 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/kg/min}} = 684 \text{ mg/min}
   \]

4. Convert the infusion time from minutes to hours:
   \[
   684 \text{ mg/min} \times \frac{1 \text{ hour}}{60 \text{ min}} = 11.4 \text{ hours}
   \]

Thus, the dose of phenytoin should be administered over 11.4 hours.

