What is the coordination geometry of the metal ion in the active site of hemoglobin, and how does this geometry enable the binding and release of oxygen molecules?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The metal ion in the active site of hemoglobin is iron (Fe), and its coordination geometry is a distorted octahedral geometry. This geometry is essential for the binding and release of oxygen molecules.

