Calculate the entropy change (J/mol K) of the given reaction. The molar entropies [J/K mol] are given in brackets after each substance.

\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} [91.2] + 3 \text{O}_2(g) [205.1] \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} [66.5] + 2 \text{SO}_2(g) [248.2] \]
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To calculate the entropy change of the reaction, we use the formula:

\[
\Delta S_{\text{reaction}} = \sum \Delta S_{\text{products}} - \sum \Delta S_{\text{reactants}}
\]

For the given reaction:

1. **Calculate the entropy of the products:**
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{products}} = 2 \times \Delta S_{\text{PbO}} + 2 \times \Delta S_{\text{SO}_2} = 2 \times 66.5 + 2 \times 248.2 = 133.0 + 496.4 = 629.4 \, \text{J/K mol}
   \]

2. **Calculate the entropy of the reactants:**
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{reactants}} = 2 \times \Delta S_{\text{PbS}} + 3 \times \Delta S_{\text{O}_2} = 2 \times 91.2 + 3 \times 205.1 = 182.4 + 615.3 = 797.7 \, \text{J/K mol}
   \]

3. **Compute the entropy change of the reaction:**
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{reaction}} = \Delta S_{\text{products}} - \Delta S_{\text{reactants}} = 629.4 - 797.7 = -168.3 \, \text{J/K mol}
   \]

The entropy change of the reaction is \(\boxed{-168.3 \, \text{J/K mol}}\).

