- A negative ΔH° indicates an exothermic reaction, where heat is released (heat is released to the surroundings, so the products are more stable than the reactants).  
- A positive ΔH° indicates an endothermic reaction, where heat is absorbed (heat is absorbed from the surroundings, so the products are less stable than the reactants).  

