","To determine the common difference, we can use the formula for the nth term of an arithmetic series:  
\[ a_n = a_1 + (n - 1)d \]  
Given \( a_1 = 19 \) and the series becomes negative at the 6th term (\( a_6 < 0 \)), we can set up the equation:  
