","To find the angle between the central maximum and the third order maximum, we use the grating formula:

\[
\sin \theta = \frac{m\lambda}{d}
\]

where:
- \(\theta = 90^\circ\) (angle of the maximum)
- \(m = 3\) (order of the maximum)
- \(\lambda = 600 \times 10^{-9} \, \text{m}\) (wavelength of the light)
- \(d = \frac{1}{800} \times 10^{-3} \, \text{m}\) (distance between the slits)

Substitute the values:

\[
\sin \theta = \frac{3 \times 600 \times 10^{-9}}{1/800 \times 10^{-3}}
\]

\[
\sin \theta = \frac{1.8 \times 10^{-6}}{1 \times 10^{-3}} = 0.0018
\]

\[
\theta = \sin^{-1}(0.0018) \approx 0.11^\circ
\]

Thus, the angle between the central maximum and the third order maximum is \(\boxed{0.11^\circ}\).
