ΔG°(hydrolysis) = -(-30.5 kJ/mol)

ΔG°(hydrolysis) = 30.5 kJ/mol

Now, we need to find the actual free energy change (ΔG) under the given conditions. We can do this using the Gibbs free energy equation:

ΔG = ΔG° + RT ln(Q)

