1. The normal component of the magnetic field \( H \) is continuous at the interface:
   \[
   H_1 \parallel = H_2 \parallel
   \]
   where \( H_1 \parallel \) and \( H_2 \parallel \) are the normal components of the magnetic field in the first and second media, respectively.

